Generated names in the verifier's Boogie program, such as those of bound variables, locals, lets, labels and proof-dependency ids, no longer embed the hex of their module's full name (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/392). A module's names now carry `M`, six base-32 characters of the SHA-256 of its full name, and `_`; a name is lengthened only when two modules of the same program share those characters. The default module's names carry no module prefix, as before module-scoped naming. Names stay unique across the modules of a program and do not depend on resolution order. This roughly halves the printed Boogie of programs with long module names; proof results are unchanged, but resource counts can move, because the solver sees different names.
